clip-path inset() and polygon() (nonzero/evenodd) over px/dp/%/calc() lengths: the
border-box region clips the element and its descendants through the clip mask, its own
filter or mask layer before it; it establishes a stacking context, limits hit testing, hides
everything when it encloses no area, and transitions between shapes of one function
(CSS Masking 1 §5, CSS Shapes 1).

